{
  "dom_id": "step-q132303",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Use trial and error to find the solutions, if any, to the congruence $4x≡5\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8).$",
  "worked_solution": "Since the modulus $n=8$ is fairly small, we can solve the congruence by trial and error. \n\nSubstituting $x=0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7$ into the equation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot 0 & ≡0≢5 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,8) &  & \\times  \\\\ 4\\cdot 1 & ≡4≢5 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,8) &  & \\times  \\\\ 4\\cdot 2 & ≡0≢5 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,8) &  & \\times  \\\\ 4\\cdot 3 & ≡4≢5 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,8) &  & \\times  \\\\ 4\\cdot 4 & ≡0≢5 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,8) &  & \\times  \\\\ 4\\cdot 5 & ≡4≢5 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,8) &  & \\times  \\\\ 4\\cdot 6 & ≡0≢5 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,8) &  & \\times  \\\\ 4\\cdot 7 & ≡4≢5 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,8) &  & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our congruence does not have any solutions.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
